# icp's audiences (core/modules/icp/README.md "Routes"): a workspace holds up to
# ICP_MAX_AUDIENCES_PER_WORKSPACE (10 unset; the list answers it as limits.audiences), its default
# among them, which the ICP's own routes act on. A member's session: icp.read for the reads,
# icp.write for the writes. `icpId` is an audience of your workspace, from the list's or the
# create's answer: put it in http-client.private.env.json with your workspaceId. Another workspace's
# id is 404 icp_not_found on every route here. A write sends the cookie, so it sends
# Origin: {{appOrigin}} too (the api's origin check).

### GET /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/icp/audiences: the workspace's audiences, the default first, then by name, and their limit; the first read makes the default
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/icp/audiences
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

### POST /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/icp/audiences: a new audience with the six default criteria; 201, or 409 icp_audience_limit past the limit
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/icp/audiences
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
Origin: {{appOrigin}}

{ "name": "Logistics founders" }

### GET /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/icp/audiences/{icpId}: the audience's name, targeting and version
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/icp/audiences/{{icpId}}
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

### PUT /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/icp/audiences/{icpId}: saves the audience; a targeting change moves its version and publishes icp.audience_updated
PUT {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/icp/audiences/{{icpId}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
Origin: {{appOrigin}}

{
  "name": "Logistics founders",
  "titles": ["Founder", "Head of Operations"],
  "seniorities": ["c_level", "director"],
  "industries": ["Logistics"],
  "sizeRanges": ["11-50"],
  "countries": ["FR"],
  "mustHaves": "Ships parcels every day.",
  "disqualifiers": "Freight brokers."
}

### GET /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/icp/audiences/{icpId}/criteria: the audience's six criteria
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/icp/audiences/{{icpId}}/criteria
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

### PUT /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/icp/audiences/{icpId}/criteria: saves the audience's six criteria; their weights sum to 100
PUT {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/icp/audiences/{{icpId}}/criteria
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
Origin: {{appOrigin}}

{
  "criteria": [
    { "key": "title_function", "weight": 30, "isMust": true, "enabled": true },
    { "key": "seniority", "weight": 15, "isMust": false, "enabled": true },
    { "key": "company_size", "weight": 10, "isMust": false, "enabled": true },
    { "key": "industry", "weight": 15, "isMust": false, "enabled": true },
    { "key": "location", "weight": 10, "isMust": true, "enabled": true },
    { "key": "must_haves", "weight": 20, "isMust": false, "enabled": true }
  ]
}
